6. **The witness** — `tests/blitz-tests/tests/local_files_for_local_documents.rs`, a new auto-discovered target.
   - It keeps arch S1–S3, tests S2–S7, security S1, obs S1 and design S1:
     - one behaviour, opened by a `//!` doc naming it;
     - descriptive test names, each test asserting its fixture's precondition first;
     - both layout modes (`for incremental in [false, true]`);
     - hand-written stand-ins, no mocking library;
     - no print, subscriber, listener, sleep or wall-clock read;
     - nothing added to the shared `fixtures` or `common` modules, which hold no `blitz_net` and no file.
   - **The stamp test.** A recording stand-in `NetProvider` keeps each request's `url` and `initiator` and answers
     nothing. It boots an `http://remote.test/page.html` document holding:
     - a `<link rel=stylesheet>`;
     - an inline `<style>` with an `@import`, an `@font-face` `src` and a `background-image`;
     - an `<img src>` and an `<iframe src>`;
     - all at `file:` URLs.
     It then calls `reload_resource_by_href` on the link's `href`. It asserts that the seven engine paths each recorded a
     request (the row count asserted: 7 distinct kinds) and that every recorded `initiator` equals the document's URL.
   - **The read-through test.** A stand-in `NetProvider` hands each request to `blitz_net::Provider::fetch_async` on a
     current-thread tokio runtime it owns (`block_on` inside `fetch`), then calls the handler's `bytes` or `error`. This
     is blitz-net's real `file:` arm, run in the test's own thread.
     - The fixture files are written by the test, their contents stated in code (tests S7), under
       `concat!(env!("CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR"), "/local_files_for_local_documents/")`:
       - a stylesheet setting `#probe`'s width to 37px;
       - an imported stylesheet setting its height to 23px;
       - a 2 × 3 PNG, written with the `png` crate;
       - a small HTML page for the `<iframe>`.
     - The same page is booted twice, through `HarnessOptions { base_url, net_provider, incremental }`:
       - base `http://remote.test/page.html`: after `settle()` reads `Ok`, `#probe` reads neither 37 wide nor 23 high,
         the `<img>` has no loaded image, and the `<iframe>` has no sub-document;
       - base `file:` (the fixture directory's `page.html`): the same readings show the width, the height, the image's
         2 × 3 size and a sub-document.
     - The `file:` URLs are built with `Url::from_file_path`, so the path form holds on Windows and macOS too.
   - The test may read the settled document only through the harness's existing readers (`layout_rect`, `base()`, the
     node's image and sub-document state). It adds no reader to the harness or the engine.

- The operator's standing directive for this wrap (`inputs#I4`):
  - P1 only;
  - the clause owed to «security-plan decision/file-script-load-refused» — the row stands in architecture (`dec-mvu7nnu6`; Spec claims disproved): P2 asks whose row takes it;
  - F1's route entry placed PROVISIONAL on A, marked waiting for the founder — P5's;
  - an escalated operation reaches the operator only with its fit verdict beside it — P2's;
  - the read-backs carry `--run-dir` — P2's.

- Guard refusals this chunk, each re-issued once in the guard's form:
  - implement: the bash-guard `cd` arm refused 2 `cd`s out of the project root (into the skill's references dir and `packages/blitz-dom/src`), re-issued with absolute paths;
  - this wrap: the pipeline arm refused `rec.py get … | sed`, re-issued bare.
